## Three.js, live: the neon city to ride, fly and walk through in a
## browser. 240 lots worked out as arrays from a seed -- another seed is
## another city -- built in the page by X_eTaL compiled to WebAssembly
## and drawn by a player written with Three.js: lit towers, neon,
## screens showing slides and videos, puddles that mirror it all, cars
## and fliers. The same arrays and the same calls as the ray-traced
## film (blender's demos/NeonCity.xtl, Cycles.xtl). From the command
## line this writes a directory to serve, work/city: the page, the
## player, Three.js and the calls.
## Run: just ext three city   (then just ext three serve city, and open
## http://127.0.0.1:8470/)
## Command: just ext three city && just ext three serve city
## Page: three/live/ fly and walk through it, live
## Title: The neon city, live
## Link: #blender-city the same city, ray-traced by Blender
## Feature: Open the city: ride, fly or walk through it in your browser

"th:" u_se< "Three"
"nc:" u_se< "NeonCity"

scene := (nc:seed, "media", 1280, 720, 30, 24, "GPU") nc:c_ity 0
"the calls of the scene, and the files written to work/city:"
th:s_how! scene
"work/city" th:p_age! scene
